# PR merge gate (agent checklist)

Lesson [#83](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/pull/83): do **not** merge with unresolved actionable bot threads.

**SSOT detail:** `CONTRIBUTING.md` → “Review check before merge”. This file is the short agent checklist only.

## Trap

**CI soft-pass ≠ merge-ready.** Gate 1 may soft-pass GitHub rate-limit (>10m / unparsable). Agents still need **either-completed** or **dual >10m**. Soft-pass ≠ on-demand/label skip.

## Decision table (gate 1 — CodeRabbit on HEAD)

| Situation | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Draft PR | CR completeness not required; still fail on unresolved bot threads. Do not merge drafts. |
| Ready + missing / pending / error / on-demand skip | **HOLD** — `@coderabbitai full review` (or label). Undraft alone does not request. |
| Ready + after fix commits | `@coderabbitai review` (incremental) |
| Local clean **or** GitHub `Review completed` | **either-completed** → OK (prefer both when available) |
| Either side can review now **or** reset **≤10m** | **WAIT/retry** that side |
| Both sides rate-limited **>10m** (or long/unknown dual) | Dual soft-pass: one-line PR note, disposition threads, merge (no rmw; no “revisit CR” issue) |
| Unilateral GitHub rate-limit; local available soon | **Not** merge-ready — wait/retry local |
| Unresolved actionable bot threads | **HOLD** unless user `rmw` / `rmcw` / `--waive` / label |

## Before merge (ordered)

1. PR **ready** (not draft).
2. Prefer both: local CR (`coderabbit review --agent` / Cursor plugin) **and** GitHub request (if not rate-limited).
3. `./scripts/check_pr_reviews.sh` (or with PR number).
4. Disposition **every** actionable finding (threads + outside-diff/summary) — see `coderabbit-lessons.mdc`.
5. Confirm either-completed **or** dual >10m; re-run script after fixes.
6. User shorthand: `rm`/`rmc` = merge for either-completed or dual >10m; `rmw`/`rmcw` = waiver for other holds; `all rmc` = loop open drafts.

## Layers (one-liner)

Local while iterating → GitHub when merge-candidate → `./scripts/check_pr_reviews.sh` + CI **Bot review threads** (status `unresolved bot threads`).
